      <h2>Frequently Asked Questions</h2>

      <h3>What is the best month to do a Spain and Morocco trip?</h3>
      <p>
        The absolute best months are <strong>April, May, September, and October</strong>. During these spring and autumn windows, southern Spain experiences glorious 22°C to 26°C (72°F to 78°F) sunshine, while the Moroccan Sahara is pleasantly warm without the brutal 42°C+ summer heat.
      </p>

      <h3>How do I handle money and currency exchange between Spain and Morocco?</h3>
      <p>
        Spain operates on the Euro (€), while Morocco uses the Moroccan Dirham (MAD). You can pay for almost everything in Spain with credit cards (Visa/Mastercard). In Morocco, while luxury riads accept cards, cash is essential for souks, tips, and café stops. We recommend withdrawing dirhams directly from bank ATMs (like Attijariwafa or BMCE) once you arrive at Tangier Port.
      </p>

      <h3>What should I pack for both Spain and Morocco?</h3>
      <p>
        Because you will be transitioning between European cosmopolitan cities and traditional Moroccan medinas, lightweight, modest layers are key. Bring comfortable walking shoes for cobblestones, a breathable scarf, linen shirts, and warm fleece layers for cool Sahara evenings. Review our complete checklist on <a href="/blog/what-to-wear-in-morocco.html"><strong>what to wear in Morocco</strong></a> and safety advice on <a href="/blog/is-morocco-safe-for-tourists.html"><strong>traveler safety in Morocco</strong></a>.
      </p>

